+# Styling Daily Grind
+
+`index.html` loads `styles.css` directly; no CSS build step is required.
+
+The cascade order is declared once: `tokens`, `base`, `layout`, `components`,
+`utilities`. Keep all author rules inside a layer: unlayered rules would outrank
+these layers. Add overrides to the appropriate layer instead of using IDs or
+`!important`.
+
+Palette primitives feed semantic color roles on `:root`, alongside the shared
+spacing, type, radius, and layout tokens. Change semantic roles to retheme the
+site. Component tokens, such as `--button-bg`, stay local to their component;
+override them in a variant rule in the components layer.
+
+Component classes define style boundaries. Shallow native nesting groups states
+and direct children; `:where()` keeps child structure from adding specificity.
+Use direct-child selectors to avoid leaking typography into embedded components.
+There is no need for proximity-based `@scope` rules in the current flat component
+tree. Introduce them if nested themes or subtree exclusions require them.
+
+Base defaults target explicit elements with low specificity rather than a
+universal reset. Use logical dimensions and spacing for writing-direction
+support. Layouts wrap intrinsically: the navigation wraps and grid tracks shrink
+below their preferred minimum when space is limited. Keep motion optional through
+the reduced-motion rule in the final layer.
